<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alphonse de Lamartine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1790">1790</a>–<a href="/years/1869">1869</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alphonse de Lamartine was a French Romantic poet and politician. In February 1848 he proclaimed the Second Republic from the Hôtel de Ville and led its provisional government as foreign minister, helping abolish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in the colonies. He stood in the presidential election of December 1848 but received few votes against Louis-Napoléon Bonaparte.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alphonse-de-lamartine.jpg" alt="Alphonse de Lamartine" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François Gérard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alphonse_de_Lamartine_par_Fran%C3%A7ois_G%C3%A9rard.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
